UID:cb9200d1d35af1d241e9a3ad024c6e4c@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Inviting 2 Spirit\, trans\, non-binary and gender diverse folk
 s of all ages to The 519 Trans Care Fair\, a day of community caring\, sha
 ring and learning. Join us Sunday\, May 10 from 12 to 4 p.m. This event is
  drop-in style\, but RSVPs are appreciated to help us estimate attendance.
  RSVP at transcarefair.eventbrite.ca. This is a trans-centred event\, and 
 allies are welcome to attend. Look forward to: - Community referrals - Sex
 ual and mental health connections and pathways to gender affirming care. -
  Workshops on trans wellness\, self-defense\, and heels dancing - Vaccinat
 ion clinic offered by Maggie&#x27\;s Toronto - Community lunch Questions o
 r access needs? Email Bernardo: BMorais@The519.org. [Image description: Gr
 oup of people walking down the street wrapped in trans flags at a past Tra
 ns March. Flowers\, shooting stars and flags in the non-binary\, intersex\
 , and trans flag colours. Text reads: &quot\;Trans Care Fair. Sunday\, May
  10\, 12 to 4 p.m. A day of community caring\, sharing\, and learning. Fre
 e\, drop in\, RSVP appreciated.&quot\;] ‍
LOCATION:The 519 Community Centre\, 519 Church Street
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/trans-care-fair-2
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Queen Out Comedy - A Fem &amp\; Queer Open Mic!
DTSTART:20260510T180000
DTEND:20260510T180000
UID:cc2ad5148a595e967a8fe0844cd92665@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:A night of inclusive and vibie open mic comedy for the girls\,
  gays\, and theys! Looking for stage time to try out your silly lil jokes?
  Want to hang with other fem and / or queer comedians? Just want to cure y
 our Sunday scaries with some comedy? WELL you are in luck! Join us for the
  first edition of Queen Out Open Mic Comedy! &lt\;33 The list goes out at 
 6 pm\, with sign up on a first come\, first serve basis\, with sign ups ca
 pped at 20 performers. The show starts promptly at 6 30 pm\, and will run 
 to approximately 8 30 pm (depending on the number of sign ups). This mic i
 s open to anyone that identifies as a woman\, fem\, and / or member of the
  2SLGBTQIA+ community. Sorry cis het dude comics - this one&#x27\;s not fo
 r you. You are welcome to perform\, attend as an audience member to suppor
 t fem and queer comedy\, or both!! The fine print: 5 minute sets\, &quot\;
 warning light&quot\; at 4 minutes The list will be &quot\;capped&quot\; or
  limited to 20 performers. This is to ensure we are out of the venue durin
 g our alloted time and to keep the show length manageable and pleasant. Pl
 ease arrive as early as possible to maximize your chances of getting on. F
 ree to attend with no purchase required\, BUT please support the amazing v
 enue if you can. There are a range of nonalcoholic and alcoholic beverages
  for purhcase as well as food The venue is fully accessible for mobility a
 id users including communal and single stall gender neutral washrooms at-g
 rade All ages welcome but parental / guardian company is recommended for y
 ounger performers All are welcome to watch / support this event\, includin
 g cisgender heterosexual men\, but performance spaces are open only to fem
  and / or queer folx Community guidelines are in place for this show and w
 ill be discussed at the top. This includes no &quot\;punching down&quot\;\
 , no &quot\;isms&quot\; or phobias\, and no aggressive crowd work. This mi
 c is hosted and produced by a queer\, nonbinary comedian who takes this se
 riously AF\, and who is committed to keeping the vibes cute and inclusive.
  If content of a performance isn&#x27\;t aligned with the guidelines\, the
  set will be ended early. We all want a sexy\, healthy time! You are total
 ly welcome to wear a mask. If you are feeling sick\, please stay home! Que
 stions? Want to come out but are a lil nervous? Totally feel free to reach
  out to the producer Anna Sebastien on Instagram at @annasebastiencomedy -
  its all about community! ‍
LOCATION:Society Clubhouse\, 967 College Street
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/queen-out-comedy---a-fem-queer-open-mic-2
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
