SUMMARY:Elina Filice &amp\; Maiasha - Queer Music Pride Kick-Off
DTSTART:20260602T190000
DTEND:20260602T190000
UID:f5bb074df2f28633e65468a1785d664a@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Kick off pride month with a night of queer music! Join two loc
 al singer-songwriters for a night of sapphic songs &amp\; stories. Kick of
 f pride month with a night of queer music! Join us for a night of sapphic 
 songs and stories. Two of your favorite singer-songwriters (along with spe
 cial guests) take the stage at Kensington Market’s Tapestry on June 2. E
 lina and Maiasha invite you to come dance and vibe for a night of good mus
 ic and community. Maiasha (she/her): is a queer folk singer-songwriter ori
 ginally from Minneapolis who now calls Toronto home. She is deeply connect
 ed to her queerness\, drawing inspiration from her own life in her lyrics 
 and infusing haunting imagery into her unique musical blend of folk\, pop\
 , and indie rock. Elina Filice (she/her): is a singer\, songwriter\, and s
 toryteller known for songs that defy genre and interactive live performanc
 es. Her music is soulful and melodic while being influenced by blues and s
 poken word. Now based in Toronto\, Elina has entertained audiences across 
 three continents. She regards music as a powerful tool for the queer commu
 nity. She will be launching her latest single &quot\;Bury Me&quot\; at the
  show! ‍
LOCATION:Tapestry\, 224 Augusta Ave
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/elina-filice-maiasha---queer-music-pride-k
 ick-off
